/A 1599 0 R
/Alt (The three-panel graph shows model skill. Panel a is a Taylor diagram with a horizontal axis from 0 to 1.0 and a vertical axis from 0 to 1.75, both labeled Normalized Std. Dev. Concentric arcs indicate correlation from 0.10 to 0.99. Points are numbered 1 to 33, with red circles indicating positive correlation and blue circles indicating negative correlation. Panel b is a scatter plot with a horizontal axis from minus 0.4 to 0.6 labeled Correlation coefficient and a vertical axis from 0.25 to 0.70 labeled Taylor skill score. Points are numbered 1 to 33 and colored by Standard deviation ratio, ranging from 0.75 to 2.50. The points show a general increasing trend in Taylor skill score as the correlation coefficient increases. Panel c is a scatter plot with a horizontal axis from 0.5 to 3.0 labeled Standard deviation ratio and a vertical axis from 0.25 to 0.70 labeled Taylor skill score. Points are numbered 1 to 33 and colored by Correlation coefficient, ranging from minus 0.4 to 0.6. The points show a general decreasing trend in Taylor skill score as the standard deviation ratio increases beyond 1.0.)
/K 32
/P 33 0 R
/Pg 14 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
