/Alt (The six-panel map series, arranged in two rows of three, displays precipitation distribution across a geographical region. Each panel includes a mean precipitation value in millimeters per day. Panel CMIP Historical 1951 to 2014 shows a mean of 2.59 millimeters per day. Panel SSP1-2.6 2015 to 2100 shows a mean of 2.68 millimeters per day. Panel SSP2-4.5 2015 to 2100 shows a mean of 2.94 millimeters per day. Panel APH&#132;R&#132;O&#132;D&#132;ITE 1951 to 2014 shows a mean of 2.68 millimeters per day. Panel SSP3-7.0 2015 to 2100 shows a mean of 2.71 millimeters per day. Panel SSP5-8.5 2015 to 2100 shows a mean of 3.05 millimeters per day. A horizontal legend below the maps indicates precipitation in millimeters per day, with values from 0 to 9, represented by increasing shades of dark. The maps show higher precipitation in the eastern and southern parts of the region.)
