/Alt (The two panel figure shows precipitation trends. Panel a, titled Precipitation Trend in millimeters per day per decade, displays five maps of a landmass with latitude and longitude coordinates. The maps are CMIP Historical 1951 to 2014, APH&#132;R&#132;O&#132;D&#132;ITE 1951 to 2014, SSP1-2.6 2015 to 2100, SSP3-7.0 2015 to 2100, and SSP5-8.5 2015 to 2100. Each map shows a regional precipitation trend value. Panel b, titled Regional Average Trends 1951 to 2100, is a line graph with Year on the horizontal axis from 1950 to 2100 and Regional Average Precipitation in millimeters per day on the vertical axis from 1.5 to 4.0. A legend lists six lines: CMIP Historical 0.001 millimeters per day per decade, APH&#132;R&#132;O&#132;D&#132;ITE 0.023 millimeters per day per decade, SSP1-2.6 0.031 millimeters per day per decade, SSP2-4.5 0.039 millimeters per day per decade, SSP3-7.0 0.052 millimeters per day per decade, and SSP5-8.5 0.086 millimeters per day per decade. The graph shows historical data from 1950 to 2005 and future projections from 2005 to 2100. The historical lines show relatively stable precipitation. The future projection lines show increasing precipitation trends, with SSP5-8.5 having the steepest increase.)
/K 5
/P 33 0 R
/Pg 18 0 R
