/Alt (The graph displays probability density distributions for Consecutive Dry Days, CDD, and Consecutive Wet Days, CWD. The horizontal axis represents Consecutive Days from 0 to 250. The left vertical axis shows Probability Density CDD from 0.00 to 0.08. The right vertical axis shows Probability Density CWD from 0.00 to 0.07. For CDD, a solid black line represents CDD Historical, peaking near 10 days with a probability density of 0.08. A dashed red line shows CDD SSP2-4.5, peaking near 5 days with a probability density of 0.08. A dotted red line shows CDD SSP5-8.5, peaking near 5 days with a probability density of 0.07. A horizontal arrow labeled Shift points left from the CDD Historical peak to the CDD SSP2-4.5 peak. A dotted vertical line at approximately 15 days marks the 95th Percentile. A shaded red area from approximately 15 to 75 days indicates CDD Extreme. For CWD, a solid black line represents CWD Historical, peaking near 230 days with a probability density of 0.06. A dashed blue line shows CWD SSP2-4.5, peaking near 210 days with a probability density of 0.07. A dotted blue line shows CWD SSP5-8.5, peaking near 200 days with a probability density of 0.06. A horizontal arrow labeled Shift points left from the CWD Historical peak to the CWD SSP2-4.5 peak. A shaded blue area from approximately 190 to 250 days indicates CWD Extreme.)
