/Alt (Maps shows projected wet to dry conditions over the HKH region. The horizontal axis has two main sections, SSP2-4.5 and SSP5-8.5, each containing two columns of heatmaps. The vertical axis has three sections: Near, Mid, and Far. The Near row shows heatmaps for 2021 to 2030 and 2031 to 2040. The Mid row shows heatmaps for 2041 to 2050 and 2051 to 2060. The Far row shows heatmaps for 2081 to 2090 and 2091 to 2100. A horizontal legend at the bottom indicates values from minus 3 to 3. Values from minus 3 to minus 1 are represented by darker to lighter orange and red. A value of 0 is represented by white. Values from 1 to 3 are represented by lighter to darker blue. For SSP2-4.5, Near shows predominantly orange and red, indicating drier conditions. Mid shows mostly white and light blue, indicating near normal to slightly wetter conditions. Far shows predominantly darker blue, indicating significantly wetter conditions. For SSP5-8.5, Near shows predominantly orange and red, indicating drier conditions. Mid shows mostly white and light blue, indicating near normal to slightly wetter conditions. Far shows predominantly darker blue, indicating significantly wetter conditions, with a stronger blue intensity than SSP2-4.5. )
/K 4
/P 33 0 R
/Pg 20 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
