/A 1673 0 R
/Alt (The two panel figure shows precipitation return levels. Panel a contains two maps of a landmass, each displaying a 10-year return level in millimeters per day. The top map is for SSP2-4.5, showing a range from 0 to 400 millimeters per day, with higher values in the western and eastern regions. The bottom map is for SSP5-8.5, also showing a range from 0 to 400 millimeters per day, with higher values in the western and eastern regions, and a broader area of high values in the west compared to the top map. A horizontal legend below the maps indicates values from 0 to 400 millimeters per day. Panel b is a box plot with a vertical axis labeled millimeters per day from 0 to 1400. The horizontal axis shows 10-year, 30-year, and 100-year return levels. Four box plots are grouped at each return level, representing SSP1-2.6, SSP2-4.5, SSP3-7.0, and SSP5-8.5. For the 10-year return level, the median values are around 200 to 250 millimeters per day, with SSP1-2.6 showing the highest median. For the 30-year return level, median values are similar, but the spread and maximum values increase. For the 100-year return level, median values remain similar, but the spread and maximum values increase further, with some outliers reaching 1400 millimeters per day. )
/K 6
/P 33 0 R
/Pg 20 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
